      "message": "So if I understand it correctly, we explicitly want int and float literals to have the same coercion cost so the compiler cannot tell which to choose, thus forcing the user to explicitly cast (as we discussed)? Otherwise the design of SKSL is that it always chooses the lowest coercion cost?",
